{"title":"Career roadmap · Research Associate","role":"Research Associate","summary":"A Research Associate in Materials Science/Nanoscience supports research involving the design, synthesis, processing, characterisation, modelling and application of advanced materials and nanomaterials.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[{"type":"table","header":["Item","Details"],"rows":[[{"text":"Starts"},{"text":"Year 1 UG · 2026"}],[{"text":"Degree"},{"text":"B.Sc – General / Honours"}],[{"text":"Course"},{"text":"Materials Science / Nanoscience"}],[{"text":"Desired career"},{"text":"Research Associate"}],[{"text":"Career cluster"},{"text":"Materials Science · Nanotechnology · R&D"}],[{"text":"Primary work"},{"text":"Materials synthesis, testing, characterisation, analysis and research documentation"}],[{"text":"Key skills"},{"text":"Materials science, chemistry, physics, nanoscience, laboratory techniques, Python and scientific writing"}]]}],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Research Associate — Materials Science / Nanoscience"},{"type":"p","text":"A Research Associate in Materials Science/Nanoscience supports research involving the design, synthesis, processing, characterisation, modelling and application of advanced materials and nanomaterials."},{"type":"p","text":"This is a strong academic alignment, but there is an important qualification distinction: after a B.Sc, students will more commonly enter through Research Assistant, Project Assistant, Laboratory Assistant or R&D Trainee positions. Many Research Associate positions, particularly in universities and national laboratories, require a master's degree, relevant research experience or a specific project qualification."}]},{"heading":"Recommended route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Materials Science/Nanoscience","Research Internship","Research Assistant/Project Assistant","M.Sc/M.Tech/MS","Research Associate","Scientist/Researcher"]}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Focus","Expected outcome"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build scientific and laboratory foundations"},{"text":"Research-ready graduate"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"PG + research experience"},{"text":"Research Associate / R&D professional"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Advanced specialisation"},{"text":"Senior Research Associate / Scientist"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Research leadership"},{"text":"Principal Scientist / R&D Lead / Research Manager"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Physics, chemistry, mathematics"},{"text":"University + NPTEL","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"text":"Laboratory records"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Atomic structure, bonding, solid-state fundamentals"},{"text":"University + NPTEL"},{"text":"Materials mini-project"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Crystallography, thermodynamics, phase diagrams"},{"text":"University + NPTEL"},{"text":"Phase-diagram analysis"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Nanomaterials and synthesis"},{"text":"University/research laboratory"},{"text":"Supervised synthesis project"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Materials characterisation"},{"text":"Laboratory + research papers"},{"text":"Characterisation report"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Python + scientific data analysis"},{"text":"NPTEL + projects"},{"text":"Materials-data project"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 1"},{"text":"Research internship + specialisation"},{"text":"Research laboratory/industry"},{"text":"Internship project"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 2"},{"text":"Dissertation + scientific writing"},{"text":"Faculty/research mentor"},{"text":"Dissertation + presentation"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Core Materials Science"},{"type":"p","text":"Master the relationship:"},{"type":"flow","i